{"answer":"AUD_PWM is an output, 1 bit wide, and is high-impedance during reset.","quote":"- {name: CPU_RESETN, dir: in, width: 1, async: true, pins: [C12], iostandard: LVCMOS33}
- {name: AUD_PWM, dir: out, width: 1, note: "open drain style: pulled low or high impedance, never driven high", pins: [A11], iostandard: LVCMOS33}
effect: "gain 2068, sample 0, PWM counter 0 and duty 512"
- 10-bit counter; duty = 512 + (sample_out >>> 7) latched when the counter wraps (reset value 512); AUD_PWM pulled low while counter >= duty, otherwise high impedance (the board pull-up makes it high)"}
